// Generated from the website by scripts/sync-native-documents.mjs. Do not edit by hand.
export const nativeDocuments = {"privacy":"<div class=\"min-h-screen bg-[var(--bg-primary)] pt-24 pb-16\"><div class=\"container mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5\"><div class=\"mb-8\"><p class=\"text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary\">Legal</p><h1 class=\"mt-2 text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black font-heading uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--text-primary)]\">Privacy Policy</h1><p class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]\">Last updated: 18 November 2026</p><p class=\"mt-5 max-w-3xl text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-7\">This policy explains how CarMazium handles personal data across the website, iPhone and Android apps, marketplace, auctions, Partner services and MaziuM AI.</p></div><div class=\"space-y-5\"><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">1. Who we are</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>CarMazium Ltd is the controller of personal data processed through CarMazium unless another party is clearly identified as the controller for a particular service.</p><p>Company number: 17053307. Registered in England and Wales. Contact: <a class=\"text-primary underline\" href=\"mailto:info@carmazium.com\">info@carmazium.com</a>.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">2. Who can use CarMazium</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>CarMazium accounts are for people aged 18 or over who are legally capable of entering into contracts. Business users must be authorised to act for the relevant business.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">3. Information we collect</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>Depending on how you use CarMazium, we may process:</p><ul><li>account and contact information such as name, email address, telephone number, profile image and authentication identifiers;</li><li>location information such as town, postcode and, only when you choose the “Locate Me” feature, device location used to determine a nearby postcode;</li><li>vehicle and listing information including registration, mileage, specification, condition, photographs, videos, pricing, bids, offers, handover evidence and transaction history;</li><li>business and verification information for Partner Accounts, including company or sole-trader details, address, identity evidence and documents submitted for KYC or service-provider verification;</li><li>service, warranty and insurance enquiry information that you choose to submit;</li><li>for a guest vehicle enquiry, your name, email address, optional phone number and message. We confirm your email before sharing these details with the seller of the selected vehicle so they can reply directly. This does not create an account or sign you up for marketing. Unconfirmed requests are removed after one day and guest enquiries after 90 days. Dealers may retain the resulting customer correspondence and CRM lead as needed under their own privacy responsibilities;</li><li>for a finance referral, your name, email address, phone number, selected vehicle and the time you agreed to the referral notice. These details are saved and emailed to the CarMazium admin team for follow-up before you continue to the application on Jigsaw Finance’s website. We do not send these details to a panel of finance providers or put them in the redirect URL. You enter the separate finance application directly with Jigsaw under its own privacy policy. Referral contact details are removed from our application database after 90 days; related correspondence is retained only as needed under our retention policy;</li><li>payment and payout information. Card payments are processed by Stripe. CarMazium does not receive or store full card numbers. Bank or payout details may be stored where needed to make or administer a payout;</li><li>messages, chat attachments, reports, disputes and customer-support communications;</li><li>push-notification tokens and notification preferences;</li><li>technical and usage information such as session identifiers, device/browser information, page or screen activity, referral information and analytics events; and</li><li>MaziuM AI prompts when you use separate AI features, and ordinary questions sent to the official CarMazium support chat where MaziuM responds by default unless AI replies are paused or the conversation is transferred to staff.</li></ul><p>On iPhone and Android, CarMazium uses the system picker when you choose a photo or document, requests foreground location only when you tap “Locate Me”, and requests notification permission for push alerts. The production app does not require camera, microphone, contacts, call-log, SMS, broad photo/video-library access or background-location permission for its current functionality.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">4. Why we use personal data</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>We use personal data to operate the marketplace, create and secure accounts, publish listings, run auctions, connect buyers and sellers, administer Partner services, process CarMazium fees and incentives, provide customer support, detect fraud and misuse, verify users and businesses, send service notifications, improve the platform and comply with legal obligations.</p><p>Our legal bases may include performance of a contract, steps taken at your request before entering a contract, compliance with legal obligations, our legitimate interests in operating and protecting the marketplace, and consent where consent is required.</p><p>For routine enquiries to the official CarMazium support chat, we use MaziuM AI by default under our legitimate interests in responding promptly to general questions and operating an efficient customer service function. We balance those interests with users’ expectations and privacy rights, limit third-party AI processing to relevant enquiries and minimal authorised status information, and provide a simple ability to pause AI or ask for a person. Customers can contact us about an objection or request human handling at any time.</p><p>Where we distribute an active vehicle listing to an approved automotive marketplace, dealer-research or referral partner, this is intended to help the seller reach relevant motor-trade buyers and to let authorised dealers research stock. We assess whether performance of the listing contract and/or our legitimate interests in effective vehicle advertising and dealer discovery is an appropriate lawful basis. For processing relying on legitimate interests, we must document a purpose, necessity and balancing assessment, including reasonable expectations and the rights of any identifiable seller or keeper, before enabling the relevant feed. SimpleDMS must independently assess its own lawful basis for dealer research and permitted historical vehicle observations. Uploading a listing grants a publication licence under the Terms; it is not automatically UK GDPR consent to every separate recipient and later processing purpose.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">5. AI and third-party processors</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>CarMazium uses service providers to operate the platform. These may include Supabase for authentication and data services, Stripe for payments and payouts, Vercel and Fly.io for hosting/infrastructure, Expo for mobile push-notification infrastructure, Apple and Google for sign-in where you choose those options, and OpenAI for MaziuM AI functionality.</p><p>In the official customer-support chat, MaziuM is an identified automated assistant and is active by default for routine questions. Relevant conversation messages and minimal account status may be sent to OpenAI to prepare the answer. When signed in, read-only tools can check your account role, dealer permissions, recent owned listings and auction bonus stages. These tools do not disclose bank details, contact details, private documents or other customers’ records, and cannot move money or change your account. A saved payout stage is not confirmation from your bank. Messages that appear to contain sensitive personal information, payment credentials, fraud reports, complaints needing decisions or a request for a human are routed for staff review without sending their contents to the external generative AI model. Automated answers cannot approve payouts, refunds, finance or identity decisions. You can pause AI from the support chat’s Options menu or simply ask to speak to a person. Your message remains in the same support conversation for staff to review.</p><p>The website MaziuM assistant is also enabled by default when you choose to chat, with AI privacy and Pause AI controls. An existing pause is respected. Search, AI-assisted listing descriptions, native app AI and live vehicle-specification enrichment retain their separate controls as applicable. Core DVLA/MOT lookup remains available without AI enrichment. Do not enter passwords, one-time codes, card numbers or unnecessary sensitive personal information in any chat.</p><p>If you use the in-app “Report AI response” feature, CarMazium stores the reported response, associated prompt where available, reason and optional details for administrator review. AI processing in the official support chat can be paused at any time; this does not affect our ability to respond through a human agent. Other AI features retain their separate privacy controls.</p><p>We may also use vehicle-data, verification, email, analytics and communications providers where needed to deliver a feature. Providers receive only the information reasonably necessary for their role and are subject to contractual or platform safeguards as applicable.</p><p>CarMazium may also provide a restricted, authenticated vehicle feed to approved automotive marketplace, dealer-research and referral partners, such as SimpleDMS / BuySmart where that integration is enabled. Such partners are not given access to CarMazium user sessions, administration systems, payment credentials or private verification documents.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">6. Advertising, analytics and cookies</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>The website uses necessary cookies for functions such as keeping you signed in. Analytics and marketing technologies, including Google, Meta and TikTok tools where configured, are loaded only in accordance with the website consent controls.</p><p>You can review or change website cookie choices through Cookie Preferences. See our <a class=\"text-primary underline\" href=\"/cookie-policy\">Cookie Policy</a> for more detail.</p><p>We use Google AdSense to display third-party advertisements on eligible public pages. Google and its advertising partners may process IP addresses, device/browser information, advertising identifiers and interactions with advertisements, and may use cookies or similar technologies, subject to the applicable consent choices. Personalised advertising may use information about visits to this and other websites. Google&#x27;s consent message provides advertising-partner and purpose choices for visitors in the UK, EEA and Switzerland. Use the privacy and cookie settings link provided with that message to manage or withdraw those choices. Read <a class=\"text-primary underline\" href=\"https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">7. Sharing information with other users and approved automotive partners</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>Information you intentionally publish in a vehicle listing or public profile may be visible to other users or visitors. Contact details and documents are disclosed only where the relevant product flow permits it.</p><p>For an approved vehicle-distribution or dealer-research integration, CarMazium may share selected active-Listing information such as the auction/listing reference, vehicle make/model/variant/year, mileage and specification, auction timing/status, starting bid, current valid bid where authorised, registration where required for server-side vehicle matching, broad town/region, approved public vehicle photographs, and a CarMazium source or referral link.</p><p>These partner feeds must not include seller, buyer or bidder identity/contact information, reserve price, private KYC or handover material, payment information, internal CarMazium valuations, exact seller address, or VIN unless a later feature is separately assessed and disclosed.</p><p>Live partner inventory must be refreshed and removed when it is no longer live; the proposed SimpleDMS live display becomes stale after 15 minutes, and its separate restricted live cache has a 24-hour cleanup ceiling. If the limited SimpleDMS / BuySmart historical-record licence is legally approved and enabled, permitted protected vehicle-matching and minimal auction-event observations (for example, original mileage, repeat appearances and time-stamped changed bid observations) may be retained for up to 36 calendar months from the vehicle&#x27;s last permitted CarMazium observation. Separately issued evidence reports may be retained for up to 36 months from original issue. These are upper limits under the partner arrangement, not a promise that every listing is shared or retained for the maximum period. Historical evidence cannot be presented as proof of a completed sale or actual transaction price. Under this arrangement raw registration, seller/bidder identity, reserve prices, photographs and photograph URLs are excluded from historical records and saved reports.</p><p>Partner distribution and any historical processing remain disabled until the required privacy, contractual and security approvals are completed. For listings created before the new notices take effect, we will assess compatibility with the original collection purpose and provide appropriate prior notice; existing terms alone are not treated as proof of specific consent for a newly introduced partner-history purpose.</p><p>Private member-to-member chats are intended for the participants. A specific message and attachment may be shared with CarMazium moderators when a participant reports it, and relevant records may be reviewed when needed for a dispute, safety, fraud or legal issue.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">8. International transfers</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>Some service providers may process data outside the United Kingdom. Where UK data-protection law requires safeguards for an international transfer, we use an appropriate transfer mechanism or rely on another lawful transfer basis.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">9. Retention</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>We keep personal data only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected and for legal, tax, accounting, fraud-prevention, security, dispute or regulatory requirements.</p><p>Successful account deletion removes the sign-in identity, sensitive KYC documents, account-owned files and transient personal records, withdraws unfinished listings and irreversibly anonymises the application account used as a reference by shared marketplace records.</p><p>Completed transaction, payment, bid, offer, sale, dispute, moderation, service and transactional-chat records may be retained in pseudonymous form where they remain necessary to protect other users, administer refunds or payouts, establish or defend legal claims, prevent fraud, meet financial-record obligations or comply with law. Private chat attachments are removed. When a retention purpose expires, the remaining record should be deleted or further anonymised.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">10. Account deletion</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>You can start account deletion in the CarMazium app or website settings. You can also use the public <a class=\"text-primary underline\" href=\"/delete-account\">Delete Account</a> page without relying on the mobile app.</p><p>If an account has a live auction or active bid, deletion may be delayed until that live commitment ends so deletion cannot be used to evade an active transaction. Once deletion completes, CarMazium removes the Supabase sign-in identity and the backend also blocks stale sessions or access tokens from restoring the deleted account. If you cannot sign in, contact <a class=\"text-primary underline\" href=\"mailto:info@carmazium.com?subject=Account%20deletion%20request\">info@carmazium.com</a> from the email address connected to the account.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">11. Your rights</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>Subject to applicable law and exemptions, you may have rights to access personal data, correct inaccurate data, request deletion, restrict or object to certain processing, receive portable data and withdraw consent where processing relies on consent.</p><p><strong>Right to object to legitimate-interests processing:</strong> where we or an approved automotive partner rely on legitimate interests for listing distribution or vehicle-history research, you may object at any time. We will assess and respond under applicable law, including whether processing must cease, and communicate appropriate suppression/correction to the partner. Requests to stop use of personal data for direct marketing are treated under the stronger applicable right to object. You may also request correction of inaccurate observations, including any mistaken vehicle match.</p><p>To exercise a privacy right or raise an objection about partner distribution, email <a class=\"text-primary underline\" href=\"mailto:info@carmazium.com?subject=Partner%20listing%20privacy%20request\">info@carmazium.com</a>. Where the request concerns SimpleDMS&#x27;s own processing, you may also contact <a class=\"text-primary underline\" href=\"mailto:info@simpledms.co.uk?subject=CarMazium%20data%20privacy%20request\">info@simpledms.co.uk</a>. We may need to verify your identity before acting on a request.</p><p>You may also raise a concern with the UK Information Commissioner’s Office if you believe your data-protection rights have been infringed.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">12. Security</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>We use technical and organisational safeguards intended to protect personal data, including access controls, authenticated application routes, private storage for sensitive verification evidence where implemented, and encrypted network transport. No internet service can guarantee absolute security.</p></div></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 md:p-8\"><h2 class=\"text-xl font-black text-[var(--text-primary)]\">13. Changes to this policy</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)] [&amp;_ul]:list-disc [&amp;_ul]:space-y-2 [&amp;_ul]:pl-6\"><p>We may update this Privacy Policy when the platform, our providers or legal requirements change. Material changes will be communicated where appropriate. The current version will always be published on this page.</p></div></section></div><div class=\"mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3\"><a href=\"/terms\" class=\"rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-default)] px-5 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] hover:border-primary/50\">Terms &amp; Conditions</a><a href=\"/cookie-policy\" class=\"rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-default)] px-5 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] hover:border-primary/50\">Cookie Policy</a><a href=\"/delete-account\" class=\"rounded-xl border border-red-500/30 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-red-400 hover:bg-red-500/5\">Delete Account</a></div></div></div>","partner":"<main class=\"mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-12\"><div class=\"max-w-3xl\"><p class=\"font-bold text-primary\">CarMazium for business</p><h1 class=\"mt-3 text-3xl font-black sm:text-5xl\">Know the steps before you join.</h1><p class=\"mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--text-secondary)]\">One Partner Account for motor dealers, sole traders and automotive businesses. Start with the tools you need, then add approved services as your business grows.</p><div class=\"mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3\"><a href=\"/auth/signup?role=DEALER\" class=\"rounded-xl bg-primary px-6 py-3 font-bold text-white\">Create Partner Account</a><a href=\"/pricing/traders\" class=\"rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-default)] px-6 py-3 font-bold\">See trader pricing</a><a href=\"/auth/login?redirect=%2Fdashboard%2Fpartner\" class=\"px-3 py-3 text-primary underline\">Already registered? Sign in</a></div></div><section class=\"mt-12\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold\">How registration works</h2><ol class=\"mt-5 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2\"><li class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6\"><p class=\"text-sm font-bold text-primary\">Step 1</p><h3 class=\"mt-2 text-lg font-bold\">Create and confirm your account</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]\">Choose Partner Account, enter your contact details and confirm your email. Complete your profile so we can contact you about your account.</p></li><li class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6\"><p class=\"text-sm font-bold text-primary\">Step 2</p><h3 class=\"mt-2 text-lg font-bold\">Add your business details</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]\">Choose your business type: registered company or sole trader. Complete the relevant verification fields and upload the requested evidence through your dashboard.</p></li><li class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6\"><p class=\"text-sm font-bold text-primary\">Step 3</p><h3 class=\"mt-2 text-lg font-bold\">Complete verification</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]\">Business/KYC approval is needed before dealer auction bidding is enabled. The one-time £1 account verification is reused when you add services; it is not a new charge for each service. Your dashboard shows anything still required.</p></li><li class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6\"><p class=\"text-sm font-bold text-primary\">Step 4</p><h3 class=\"mt-2 text-lg font-bold\">Choose your business tools</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7 text-[var(--text-secondary)]\">Create retail listings and manage your stock. Add delivery or inspection capabilities if you want to provide those services. Paid service work requires the relevant approval and payout setup.</p></li></ol></section><section class=\"mt-12\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold\">What to prepare</h2><div class=\"mt-5 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2\"><article class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6\"><h3 class=\"mt-3 text-xl font-bold\">Registered motor dealer</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7\">Have your registered business name, company details, representative details and the requested identity and business evidence ready. The verification form explains the documents that apply to your business.</p></article><article class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6\"><h3 class=\"mt-3 text-xl font-bold\">Sole trader</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7\">Use your trading name and owner details. Sole traders do not need a Companies House registration. Prepare photo ID, recent proof of address and the sole-trader evidence requested by the verification form.</p></article><article class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6\"><h3 class=\"mt-3 text-xl font-bold\">Delivery, collection and recovery</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7\">Complete your business declaration, provide trade insurance covering the work and set up secure business payouts. Existing approved dealer verification is reused. Upload only the evidence requested for this service.</p></article><article class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6\"><h3 class=\"mt-3 text-xl font-bold\">Vehicle inspections</h3><p class=\"mt-3 leading-7\">Complete your business details, declaration and verified payout setup. The inspection service setup does not require document uploads or formal certificates. Providers remain responsible for competent work and appropriate insurance.</p></article></div><p class=\"mt-4 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]\">Submit documents and bank details only through the secure account setup. Do not email them. Approval depends on the information supplied; we do not promise a fixed review time.</p></section><section class=\"rounded-2xl border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-card)] p-6 mt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold\">Finance, warranty and insurance providers</h2><p class=\"mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-7\">These partnerships and integrations are arranged directly with the CarMazium team. Tell us which service your business provides so we can explain the appropriate next steps.</p><div class=\"mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-4\"><a href=\"/contact?topic=finance-partnership\" class=\"rounded-lg border border-primary px-4 py-3 font-semibold capitalize text-primary\">Discuss finance partnership</a><a href=\"/contact?topic=warranty-partnership\" class=\"rounded-lg border border-primary px-4 py-3 font-semibold capitalize text-primary\">Discuss warranty partnership</a><a href=\"/contact?topic=insurance-partnership\" class=\"rounded-lg border border-primary px-4 py-3 font-semibold capitalize text-primary\">Discuss insurance partnership</a></div></section><section class=\"mt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold\">What you can do—and when</h2><div class=\"mt-5 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-[var(--border-default)]\"><table class=\"w-full text-left\"><thead class=\"bg-[var(--bg-input)]\"><tr><th class=\"p-4\">Activity</th><th class=\"p-4\">What is needed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=\"border-t border-[var(--border-default)]\"><td class=\"p-4 font-semibold\">Create retail listings</td><td class=\"p-4\">Partner Account and the usual listing details and publication/payment steps.</td></tr><tr class=\"border-t border-[var(--border-default)]\"><td class=\"p-4 font-semibold\">Bid in dealer auctions</td><td class=\"p-4\">Approved motor-trader business/KYC verification.</td></tr><tr class=\"border-t border-[var(--border-default)]\"><td class=\"p-4 font-semibold\">Provide delivery or inspection services</td><td class=\"p-4\">Relevant service approval, business declaration and payout setup.</td></tr><tr class=\"border-t border-[var(--border-default)]\"><td class=\"p-4 font-semibold\">Provide finance, warranty or insurance</td><td class=\"p-4\">A partnership arranged directly with our team.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><div class=\"mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4\"><a href=\"/auth/signup?role=DEALER\" class=\"rounded-xl bg-primary px-6 py-3 font-bold text-white\">Create Partner Account</a><a href=\"/contact\" class=\"px-4 py-3 text-primary underline\">Get help choosing your account</a></div></main>","warrantyTerms":"<div class=\"container mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pt-28 pb-20 space-y-6\"><h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold\">Before you order a warranty</h1><p>CarMazium provides the platform and collects the displayed payment through Stripe. Pulse Cars Limited arranges the Warrantywise warranty as broker. CarMazium and Pulse Cars Limited do not carry out warranty repairs through this checkout.</p><h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold\">Your quote and payment</h2><p>Your quote is based on the vehicle category and options you select. All displayed prices include VAT. Check the vehicle details, current mileage, service history, repair limit, labour allowance and optional additions before paying. This payment purchases a warranty order, not the vehicle.</p><h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold\">Issuance and cover</h2><p>Payment does not immediately activate warranty cover. Admin checks the details, arranges the selected warranty and pays the supplier separately. We then send the warranty reference and confirmed cover dates. The requested start date is not a guarantee of cover before issuance.</p><p>Vehicle eligibility, covered components, service requirements, exclusions and repair authorisation are governed by the issued Warrantywise plan. A repair limit or optional addition does not mean every fault or repair is covered. Known and pre-existing faults must be disclosed. Do not authorise repairs on the assumption that this order covers them.</p><p>If we cannot arrange the selected cover, we will contact you and refund your payment. We will not substitute lower cover without discussing it with you. For cancellation or questions about an issued warranty, contact our team and refer to the cancellation terms supplied with your plan. This information does not limit your statutory rights.</p><p><a class=\"underline\" href=\"https://www.warrantywise.co.uk/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Read Warrantywise’s product and plan information</a>. Your issued plan documents confirm the terms that apply to your vehicle.</p><h2 class=\"text-xl font-bold\">Your information</h2><p>We use the details you supply to prepare the quote, take payment, arrange the warranty and send order updates. We share the necessary details with Pulse Cars Limited and Warrantywise for fulfilment. Stripe handles your card details. See our <a class=\"underline\" href=\"/privacy-policy\">Privacy Policy</a>.</p><p>Quote/order information version: 13 November 2026.</p><div class=\"flex gap-5\"><a class=\"underline\" href=\"/services/warranty\">Back to warranty quotes</a><a class=\"underline\" href=\"/contact\">Contact the team</a></div></div>"};
